Word Search II (Hard – Trie + Backtracking)

✅ This problem is NOT in your list.
It’s a very popular FAANG-level problem.

📌 PROBLEM STATEMENT

You are given:

A 2D board of characters.

A list of words.

Return all words from the list that can be formed in the board.

Rules:

Letters must be adjacent (up, down, left, right).

Same cell cannot be reused in one word.

🧾 Example
Board =
[
  ['o','a','a','n'],
  ['e','t','a','e'],
  ['i','h','k','r'],
  ['i','f','l','v']
]

Words = ["oath","pea","eat","rain"]

✅ Output:
["oath", "eat"]

🧠 WHY TRIE?

If we search each word separately → Very slow ❌
Instead:

Store all words in a Trie

Do one DFS traversal

Match prefixes efficiently

This reduces repeated work.

💡 IDEA

Build a Trie from words.

For each cell → start DFS.

Move in 4 directions.

If Trie says prefix invalid → stop early.

If complete word found → add to result.

Mark cell visited temporarily.

Backtrack.

🪜 ALGORITHM
Step 1:

Build Trie from word list.

Step 2:

Loop over every cell.

Step 3:

DFS:

Check bounds.

Check if character exists in Trie.

Move to next Trie node.

If node.word != null → found word.

Mark visited.

Explore 4 directions.

Restore cell.

💻 FULL JAVA CODE
import java.util.*;

public class WordSearchII {

    static class TrieNode {
        TrieNode[] children = new TrieNode[26];
        String word;  // Stores complete word
    }

    public static List<String> findWords(char[][] board, String[] words) {
        List<String> result = new ArrayList<>();

        TrieNode root = buildTrie(words);

        for (int i = 0; i < board.length; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < board[0].length; j++) {
                dfs(board, i, j, root, result);
            }
        }

        return result;
    }

    private static void dfs(char[][] board, int i, int j,
                            TrieNode node, List<String> result) {

        if (i < 0 || j < 0 || i >= board.length || j >= board[0].length)
            return;

        char c = board[i][j];

        if (c == '#' || node.children[c - 'a'] == null)
            return;

        node = node.children[c - 'a'];

        if (node.word != null) {
            result.add(node.word);
            node.word = null; // Avoid duplicates
        }

        board[i][j] = '#'; // Mark visited

        dfs(board, i + 1, j, node, result);
        dfs(board, i - 1, j, node, result);
        dfs(board, i, j + 1, node, result);
        dfs(board, i, j - 1, node, result);

        board[i][j] = c; // Backtrack
    }

    private static TrieNode buildTrie(String[] words) {

        TrieNode root = new TrieNode();

        for (String word : words) {

            TrieNode node = root;

            for (char c : word.toCharArray()) {

                if (node.children[c - 'a'] == null) {
                    node.children[c - 'a'] = new TrieNode();
                }

                node = node.children[c - 'a'];
            }

            node.word = word;  // Store word at leaf
        }

        return root;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        char[][] board = {
                {'o','a','a','n'},
                {'e','t','a','e'},
                {'i','h','k','r'},
                {'i','f','l','v'}
        };

        String[] words = {"oath","pea","eat","rain"};

        System.out.println(findWords(board, words));
    }
}

